Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.87,0:00:08.97,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.31,0:00:31.43,Default,,0,0,0,,You're on the move!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.45,0:01:04.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You may have destroyed my Egyptian gods,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.43,0:01:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,but defeating my Dark\NMagician is your true test.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.21,0:01:09.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, man!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.12,0:01:11.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's up against his most famous monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.83,0:01:13.95,Default,,0,0,0,,We should have sold tickets to this.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.61,0:01:16.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I never thought this day would come,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.85,0:01:19.67,Default,,0,0,0,,but I need a strategy to\Nwipe out Dark Magician.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.93,0:01:23.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the only way I can win this\Nduel and set the Pharaoh free.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.91,0:01:30.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I'll play one monster\Nface down in defense mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.15,0:01:33.89,Default,,0,0,0,,dark magician is stronger\Nthan ever now thanks to the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.97,0:01:36.63,Default,,0,0,0,,pharaoh's magic card but\Ni know that somewhere in
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.71,0:01:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,my deck there's a card that\Ncan beat it next i switch
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.87,0:01:44.95,Default,,0,0,0,,curse of dragon to defense\Nmode that ends my turn
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.03,0:01:47.93,Default,,0,0,0,,looks like all yugi can do\Nis strengthen his defenses
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.01,0:01:51.91,Default,,0,0,0,,nah i bet he's doing more\Nthan that and if you ask
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.99,0:01:55.01,Default,,0,0,0,,me The secret's in that\Nface-down monster of his.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.07,0:01:59.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that card what I think it is?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.25,0:02:03.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Whenever my Witch of the Black\NForest goes to the graveyard,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.65,0:02:06.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I can transfer a monster\Nfrom my deck to my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.87,0:02:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,And I choose my good old Marshmellon.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.01,0:02:15.25,Default,,0,0,0,,If I know Yugi as well as I think I do,\Nthe card he laid down is Marshmellon.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.39,0:02:18.79,Default,,0,0,0,,For if that monster is attacked\Nwhile face-down in defense mode,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.87,0:02:21.33,Default,,0,0,0,,the opposing player loses 1,000 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.41,0:02:26.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And with only 700 life points left,\Nif I attack it, I lose the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.35,0:02:30.01,Default,,0,0,0,,However, I have another plan in mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.73,0:02:31.77,Default,,0,0,0,,My move.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.65,0:02:37.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate the magic\Ncard, Thousand Knives!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.25,0:02:40.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Unreal.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.35,0:02:43.43,Default,,0,0,0,,He keeps drawing exactly what\Nhe needs at the right time.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.51,0:02:45.95,Default,,0,0,0,,He's controlling his deck with his will.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.03,0:02:48.29,Default,,0,0,0,,When Dark Magician is in play,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.47,0:02:53.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I can use my thousand knives to destroy\None monster on your side of the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.35,0:02:55.85,Default,,0,0,0,,So say goodbye to your face down card!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.05,0:03:01.29,Default,,0,0,0,,My Marshmellon!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.41,0:03:05.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Since it was destroyed using a magic\Ncard, its special effect doesn't activate.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.99,0:03:07.85,Default,,0,0,0,,So my life points are safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.11,0:03:10.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, my Dark Magician, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.45,0:03:19.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi! Hey, Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.35,0:03:23.97,Default,,0,0,0,,So what happened to that big strategy\Nof his you were talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.05,0:03:26.95,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll pull through just\Nonce! Yeah, but how?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.21,0:03:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It won't be easy, but there\Nis a way out of this mess.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.25,0:03:35.15,Default,,0,0,0,,The only question is, does Yugi have\Nthe cards and the guts to pull it off?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.93,0:03:41.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Dark Magician's strong,\Nbut he's not invincible!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.91,0:03:44.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Well then, let's see you take him down.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.25,0:03:49.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, I will.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.55,0:03:51.65,Default,,0,0,0,,But first, I summon this.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.73,0:03:54.27,Default,,0,0,0,,My Block Man in defense mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.35,0:03:56.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'll place one card face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.03,0:03:58.45,Default,,0,0,0,,That's all for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.35,0:04:03.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I was expecting more.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.15,0:04:07.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I activate my Dark Spear Magic Card.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.75,0:04:12.11,Default,,0,0,0,,With his Dark Spear in hand, my\NMagician gains a unique ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.19,0:04:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,If his attack points exceed\Nyour monster's defense points,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.21,0:04:19.50,Default,,0,0,0,,then the difference is\Nsubtracted from your life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.13,0:04:22.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Dark Magician, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.35,0:04:25.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Destroy his Bluffman!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.67,0:04:28.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You triggered my trap!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.71,0:04:30.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Soul Shield!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.17,0:04:35.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to my trap,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.77,0:04:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,all I had to do was sacrifice\Nhalf of my life points
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.75,0:04:41.67,Default,,0,0,0,,to negate your attack and\Nend your battle phase!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.19,0:04:45.72,Default,,0,0,0,,So your Dark Magician will have\Nto wait till your next turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.23,0:04:47.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Well executed, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.03,0:04:50.97,Default,,0,0,0,,And the tide turns again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.43,0:04:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but now Yugi only\Nhas 400 life points left.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.15,0:04:56.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Here we go.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.47,0:04:59.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time to send your Magician packing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.83,0:05:01.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.79,0:05:03.50,Default,,0,0,0,,That's exactly what I needed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.71,0:05:09.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I activate a magic card\Nknown as Gold Sarcophagus.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.49,0:05:13.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And here's how it works.\NFirst I choose a card.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.75,0:05:17.01,Default,,0,0,0,,from my deck and place\Nit into this ancient box
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.65,0:05:23.59,Default,,0,0,0,,then if you happen to activate the same\Ncard the effect of your card is negated
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.11,0:05:33.53,Default,,0,0,0,,so what card do you think he put\Nin there guys i don't know but what
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.61,0:05:36.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Are the chances the Pharaoh's\Ngoing to play the exact same card?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.01,0:05:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,That box looks just like the one\Nthe Millennium Puzzle came from.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.79,0:05:44.85,Default,,0,0,0,,So the same symbol that brought them\Ntogether might split them apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.47,0:05:50.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I activate my Bloodman's\Nspecial ability, Deconstruction!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.19,0:05:55.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Since two turns have\Npassed since I played it,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.95,0:05:58.66,Default,,0,0,0,,my Bloodman is reconfigured\Ninto two monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.95,0:06:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,And now I plan to sacrifice both of them,\Nwhich lets me play a more powerful one.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.97,0:06:08.35,Default,,0,0,0,,One that's strong enough to\Ndestroy your Dark Magician!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.69,0:06:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,So check this out!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.01,0:06:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Gandorra, the Dragon of Destruction!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.23,0:06:17.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Not bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.13,0:06:20.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Since when do you have that card?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.17,0:06:21.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I remember that monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.85,0:06:25.47,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the same monster\NYugi used to defeat.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.55,0:06:28.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Bukura when he was\Nseparated from the Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.29,0:06:33.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It proved that Yugi could win on his own,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.03,0:06:37.85,Default,,0,0,0,,So it's the perfect monster\Nto defeat the Pharaoh with. My
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.93,0:06:41.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Dragon of Destruction can only\Nremain on the field for one turn,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.57,0:06:46.51,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's all I need. So I'll pay half\Nmy life points to activate Gandora's.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.59,0:06:50.53,Default,,0,0,0,,special ability and remove every\Nmonster on the field from the game
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.23,0:06:56.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Gandora, destroy his Dark\NMagician with Boundless Giga Rage.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.77,0:07:01.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I reveal my trap, Dark Illusion!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.81,0:07:13.73,Default,,0,0,0,,My Dark Illusion Trap Card\Nshall protect my Dark Magician
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.81,0:07:18.01,Default,,0,0,0,,from all monster effects for the\Nremainder of the turd! No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.31,0:07:21.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Even with Gandor, I couldn't\Ndefeat his Dark Magician!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.73,0:07:22.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.64,0:07:24.46,Default,,0,0,0,,due to the effect of my Dark Illusion,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.55,0:07:27.31,Default,,0,0,0,,you're allowed to draw\None card from your deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.39,0:07:28.95,Default,,0,0,0,,So go ahead and draw.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.01,0:07:36.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I place these two cards face\Ndown, and that ends my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.51,0:07:40.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Now Yugi's back to having\Nno monsters to protect him.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.01,0:07:44.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I hate to say it, guys, but I\Nthink it's really over this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.65,0:07:47.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Not necessarily, Mokuba.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.91,0:07:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,The way this duel's been going\Nso far, anything can happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.89,0:07:55.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my move.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.65,0:07:59.06,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Dark Magician,\Nattack his life points directly!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.53,0:08:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate my trap!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.75,0:08:04.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Magician Circle!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.97,0:08:10.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Whenever you attack me with a spellcaster,\NI can activate this trap card!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.69,0:08:15.22,Default,,0,0,0,,And it gives me the power to automatically\Nsummon a spellcaster from my deck!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.73,0:08:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the perfect card to\Nuse against my Dark Magician.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.23,0:08:21.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew Yugi was prepared for my strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.23,0:08:25.39,Default,,0,0,0,,So now I summon my Silent Magician!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.43,0:08:33.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice move, but your Trap Card\Nallows me to play a monster as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.23,0:08:37.51,Default,,0,0,0,,So now I summon Dark Magician Girl!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.85,0:08:42.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh man, two Dark Magicians?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.39,0:08:50.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Now my Dark Magician, attack! Destroy\Nhis monster and end this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.17,0:08:57.51,Default,,0,0,0,,as soon as his dark magician attacks\Nthe pharaoh wins this can't be the end
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.71,0:09:13.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not done yet, Pharaoh If\Nyour spirit's ever gonna be free,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.63,0:09:17.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to win this duel\NI activate my magic card,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.09,0:09:19.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Spell Textbook
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.19,0:09:27.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, by discarding every card in my\Nhand I can draw one from my deck!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.61,0:09:30.61,Default,,0,0,0,,And if it's a magic card,\NI can use it right away!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.27,0:09:34.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Since my hand's empty, I\Nhave nothing to discard!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.47,0:09:39.24,Default,,0,0,0,,The card I'm about to draw will\Ndetermine the Pharaoh's destiny!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.39,0:09:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I activate this!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.47,0:09:46.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Card of Sanctity!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.17,0:09:51.35,Default,,0,0,0,,So we both have to draw until we're\Neach holding six cards in our hand!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.67,0:09:59.79,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not all. Next, I activate my\NMagician's special effect with every card.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.87,0:10:06.15,Default,,0,0,0,,you draw my silent magician's attack\Nstrength increases by 500 points and i just
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.23,0:10:12.45,Default,,0,0,0,,picked up five new cards exactly so\Nmy silent magician now has 3500 attack
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.53,0:10:17.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Points now back to the duel. I believe\Nyour Dark Magician was about to attack?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.53,0:10:23.47,Default,,0,0,0,,He's only got 700 life points, so\Nas soon as his Magician attacks,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.79,0:10:24.85,Default,,0,0,0,,the Pharaoh loses.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.07,0:10:33.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I activate my magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.53,0:10:35.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Magicians unite!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.29,0:10:38.41,Default,,0,0,0,,This allows me to join my two Magicians
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.49,0:10:42.23,Default,,0,0,0,,together as one spell\Ncaster with 3,000 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.33,0:10:49.13,Default,,0,0,0,,That's still not enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.51,0:11:05.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Very impressive, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.51,0:11:08.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Although I was able to save my\Nlife points from destruction,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.51,0:11:11.51,Default,,0,0,0,,your magician succeeded\Nin defeating both of mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.99,0:11:16.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Now we each have 200 life\Npoints left, So the end is near.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.61,0:11:18.53,Default,,0,0,0,,This will be my final turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.95,0:11:25.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You have fought bravely, but unfortunately\Nthis duel will conclude with my victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.09,0:11:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.47,0:11:30.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you tried everything\Nin your power to set me free.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.73,0:11:33.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate this.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.13,0:11:36.69,Default,,0,0,0,,The Magic Card Monster Reborn.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.97,0:11:41.81,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, I shall resurrect\NSlifer the Sky Dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.49,0:11:50.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, man!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.75,0:11:52.93,Default,,0,0,0,,He just brought back an Egyptian god!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.49,0:11:57.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Slipers' attack points are determined\Nby the number of cards in my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.67,0:12:01.53,Default,,0,0,0,,And since I'm holding four,\Nhe now has 4,000 points!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.25,0:12:06.75,Default,,0,0,0,,My spirit shall remain in this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.07,0:12:10.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess Yugi and I weren't\Ndestined to separate.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.77,0:12:14.71,Default,,0,0,0,,If I were you, I would have summoned\Nan Egyptian god also, Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.85,0:12:17.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And that's why I was prepared\Nfor this very moment!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.83,0:12:21.79,Default,,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.45,0:12:28.67,Default,,0,0,0,,The card I hid inside that box\Nis the same card you just played!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.79,0:12:36.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, but that's impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.55,0:12:39.29,Default,,0,0,0,,There's only one Slifer\Nthe Sky Dragon card!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.43,0:12:44.87,Default,,0,0,0,,The card I buried was Monster Reborn
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.45,0:12:49.61,Default,,0,0,0,,And since the magic card\Nyou just played Is the same
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.69,0:12:52.55,Default,,0,0,0,,one that I placed in my\Ngold sarcophagus The effect
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.63,0:12:56.05,Default,,0,0,0,,of your card is negated\NWhich means your Egyptian god
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.13,0:13:00.49,Default,,0,0,0,,goes back to the graveyard\NSo this duel is still on
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.53,0:13:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,No way He just defeated Slifer\Nfor the second time Of all the
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.57,0:13:11.09,Default,,0,0,0,,cards to put in that box How\Ndid Yugi know which one to pick?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.17,0:13:12.27,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you expect?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.35,0:13:14.06,Default,,0,0,0,,He's the king of games, dude.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.21,0:13:16.77,Default,,0,0,0,,He must have had this\Nplan from the beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.85,0:13:19.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess after spending so\Nmuch time with the Pharaoh,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.03,0:13:22.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi knew exactly what he would play.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.49,0:13:25.13,Default,,0,0,0,,This was the greatest duel of my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.63,0:13:27.51,Default,,0,0,0,,It's been an honor, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.19,0:13:30.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.37,0:13:31.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Your move.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.69,0:13:33.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.07,0:13:35.48,Default,,0,0,0,,What's Yugi waiting for?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.23,0:13:40.13,Default,,0,0,0,,All he has to do is attack and\Nthe duel is over. That's just it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.35,0:13:43.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Once the match comes to an end,\Nthe pharaoh will be released.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.43,0:13:45.20,Default,,0,0,0,,And we'll never see him again.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.71,0:13:49.29,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all right, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.09,0:13:50.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Proceed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.57,0:13:55.75,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Silent Magician,\Nattack his life points directly!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.39,0:14:10.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, so did Yugi win the duel?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.87,0:14:13.69,Default,,0,0,0,,If this attack is successful, then yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.55,0:14:41.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Congratulations.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.46,0:14:42.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Well done.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.49,0:14:48.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, a champion doesn't\Nbelong on his knees.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.47,0:14:51.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You achieved a great victory for us both.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.71,0:14:55.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I was focusing so hard on\Nplaying the game that I
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.35,0:14:58.47,Default,,0,0,0,,forgot what winning this\Nduel would actually mean.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.77,0:15:02.13,Default,,0,0,0,,By defeating you, I've\Nsent you away. For good.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.55,0:15:04.85,Default,,0,0,0,,No, you have opened the door for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.93,0:15:08.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to you, my spirit can\Nfinally be at rest once again.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.03,0:15:10.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be back where I belong.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.39,0:15:16.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Fate brought the two of us together for a\Nreason, and we've fulfilled our destiny.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.87,0:15:20.49,Default,,0,0,0,,We've protected mankind from\Nthe return of the Shadow Games.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.57,0:15:23.89,Default,,0,0,0,,and we've both grown\Ntremendously along the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.17,0:15:25.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna miss you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.91,0:15:29.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You do realize we'll never\Ntruly be apart, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.79,0:15:34.01,Default,,0,0,0,,The gift of kindness you've given\Nme, and the courage I've given you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.41,0:15:35.59,Default,,0,0,0,,will remain with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.75,0:15:39.05,Default,,0,0,0,,And that will forever\Nbind us together. Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.71,0:15:43.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.01,0:15:45.36,Default,,0,0,0,,What's up with the eye?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.51,0:15:47.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that the battle ritual is complete,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.13,0:15:51.91,Default,,0,0,0,,the Eye of Ujjat that guards the door\Nto the spirit world has awakened.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.99,0:15:54.23,Default,,0,0,0,,And the spirit of the great pharaoh,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.43,0:15:58.11,Default,,0,0,0,,which was trapped within the\NMillennium Puzzle for 5,000 years,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.19,0:15:59.43,Default,,0,0,0,,is now free.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.87,0:16:03.21,Default,,0,0,0,,So this is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.59,0:16:06.41,Default,,0,0,0,,The time has arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.69,0:16:08.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell the Eye of Ujjat your name.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.15,0:16:12.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I am the son of King Apnam Cannon.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.77,0:16:14.97,Default,,0,0,0,,My name is Ather.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.33,0:16:29.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Farrow!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.43,0:16:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't go!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.89,0:16:34.73,Default,,0,0,0,,So that's how it ends, huh? Nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.09,0:16:39.74,Default,,0,0,0,,You think you can just show up and change\Neverybody's life and then just leave?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.17,0:16:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,What Tristan means is we\Ndon't want to say goodbye.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.39,0:16:47.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.39,0:16:51.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Farrow, I know walking through that door\Nmeans your spirit will finally be free.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.99,0:16:55.07,Default,,0,0,0,,And it's all for the best,\Nbut it doesn't seem fair.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.59,0:16:59.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, I feel like we were\Nall just getting to know you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.27,0:17:02.31,Default,,0,0,0,,In fact, you were just beginning\Nto get to know yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.39,0:17:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,And now you're being taken away from us.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.11,0:17:07.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I know we should be happy for you,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.19,0:17:09.53,Default,,0,0,0,,but it's really hard to do that\Nwhen you're losing your best
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.61,0:17:13.32,Default,,0,0,0,,friend and you just don't understand\Nwhy it has to be that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.63,0:17:17.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess there are some things\Nwe're not supposed to understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.39,0:17:18.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Just look at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.63,0:17:21.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I go through half my life not\Nunderstanding what's going on.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.99,0:17:27.27,Default,,0,0,0,,But I know that true friends may be hard\Nto leave, but they're impossible to forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.13,0:17:31.23,Default,,0,0,0,,And even though his stay wasn't\Nas long as we would have liked,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.31,0:17:33.57,Default,,0,0,0,,we're lucky we knew him at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.23,0:17:35.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Joy.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.77,0:17:37.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Goodbye, Atem.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.19,0:17:39.15,Default,,0,0,0,,And good luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.95,0:17:40.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Pharaoh!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.27,0:17:44.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I hate to break the terrible news to\Nyou, but you're not going anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.01,0:17:48.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Because everything you've given\Nus stays right here in our hearts.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.27,0:17:50.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.18,0:17:53.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Like we always say, it's your move!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.83,0:18:26.85,Default,,0,0,0,,He's gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.77,0:18:30.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, Pharaoh, goodbye.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.75,0:18:38.55,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that? An earthquake.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.51,0:18:42.21,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the Millennium Stone!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.41,0:18:46.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The items are gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.41,0:18:47.93,Default,,0,0,0,,And we should do the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.01,0:18:51.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Run for your lives! He's right! Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.01,0:19:17.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that the Pharaoh has\Nreturned to the next world,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.61,0:19:21.09,Default,,0,0,0,,the Millennium Items have been\Npermanently sealed And our
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.17,0:19:24.41,Default,,0,0,0,,duty as the Pharaoh's Tomb\NKeepers is finally complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.61,0:19:26.07,Default,,0,0,0,,So this is the end?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.25,0:19:27.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Feels weird. Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.33,0:19:30.10,Default,,0,0,0,,What were you geeks expecting?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.81,0:19:33.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Fireworks, sappy music, something.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.51,0:19:36.03,Default,,0,0,0,,At least make one of your\Nlittle wrap-up speeches, Yug.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.11,0:19:40.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, sometimes the end of one adventure\Nis just the beginning of another.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.89,0:19:42.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, much better.
